      vulnStatus: Modified
      cveTags: []
      descriptions[1]{lang,value}:
        en,"cpio on FreeBSD 2.1.0, Debian GNU/Linux 3.0, and possibly other operating systems, uses a 0 umask when creating files using the -O (archive) or -F options, which creates the files with mode 0666 and allows local users to read or overwrite those files."
