      descriptions[1]{lang,value}:
        en,"rcp on various Linux systems including Red Hat 4.0 allows a \"nobody\" user or other user with UID of 65535 to overwrite arbitrary files, since 65535 is interpreted as -1 by chown and other system calls, which causes the calls to fail to modify the ownership of the file."
